{"slug":"ablative_case","word":"ablative case","rank":9804,"category":"communication","pos":"noun","gloss":"grammatical case used to indicate movement away from something, removal, separation, source","definitions":["A noun case used in some languages to indicate movement away from something, removal, separation. In English grammar, it corresponds roughly to the use in English of prepositions \"of\", \"from\", \"away from\", and \"concerning\". In Latin grammar, the ablative case (cāsus ablātīvus) includes functions derived from the Indo-European ablative, instrumental, comitative, associative and locative cases; these cases express concepts similar to those of the English prepositions \"of\"/\"from\", \"by\", \"with\", \"to\"/\"with\", and \"at\"/\"in\", respectively. Here/hence/hither, there/thence/thither, and where/whence/whither are the only English words with separate forms for the ablative (motion away from) and lative (motion towards) cases."],"translations":{"af":[{"w":"ablatief","src":"ai"}],"sq":[{"w":"rrjedhore"}],"am":[{"w":"የመነሻ ሁኔታ","src":"ai","r":"yämänäša hunetta","low":1}],"ar":[{"w":"حالة الإبعاد","src":"ai","r":"ḥālat al-ibʿād","low":1}],"hy":[{"w":"բացառական","r":"bacʻaṙakan"},{"w":"բացառական հոլով","r":"bacʻaṙakan holov"}],"az":[{"w":"çıxışlıq hal"}],"eu":[{"w":"ablatibo","src":"ai"}],"be":[{"w":"аблатыў","src":"ai","r":"ablatyu"}],"bn":[{"w":"অপাদান","r":"opadan"}],"bs":[{"w":"ablativ","g":"m"}],"bg":[{"w":"творителен падеж","r":"tvoritelen padež","g":"m"},{"w":"отделителен падеж","r":"otdelitelen padež"},{"w":"аблатив","r":"ablativ"}],"ca":[{"w":"ablatiu","g":"m"}],"ceb":[{"w":"ablatibo","src":"ai"}],"ny":[{"w":"kachitidwe ka dzina losonyeza kuchoka","src":"ai","low":1}],"zh-Hans":[{"w":"夺格","r":"duógé"},{"w":"离格","r":"lígé"}],"zh-Hant":[{"w":"奪格","r":"duógé"},{"w":"離格","r":"lígé"}],"co":[{"w":"casu ablativu","src":"ai"}],"hr":[{"w":"ablativ","g":"m"}],"cs":[{"w":"ablativ","g":"m"}],"da":[{"w":"ablativ","g":"c"}],"nl":[{"w":"ablatief","g":"m"